vehicles for sellers and buyers; vehicle logistics center locations; SaaS-based private label remarketing solutions to automobile manufacturers, captive finance companies, and other commercial customers to digitally offer vehicles for sale; wholesale vehicle marketplaces; and value-added ancillary services including inbound and outbound transportation logistics, reconditioning and mechanical work, vehicle inspection and certification, titling, administrative, and collateral recovery services. This segment sells its products and services through commercial fleet operators, financial institutions, car rental companies, new and used vehicle dealers, and vehicle manufacturers. Its marketplaces include OPENLANE platform, a mobile app enabled solutions that allows dealers to sell and source inventory. The Finance segment offers floorplan financing, a short-term inventory-secured financing to independent vehicle dealers; liquidity for customer trade-ins; and title services. In addition, the company provides pre- and post-sale inspection; transportation and logistics; digital marketplace services; remarketing services; and vehicle research services. It serves commercial customers, and franchise and independent dealer customers. The company was formerly known as KAR Auction Services, Inc. and changed its name to OPENLANE, Inc. in May 2023. OPENLANE, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Carmel, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter J. Kelly | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $480K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["OPENLANE, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.3B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $336M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries a 36% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.35811253627937467},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (93% sell ratio, net $280.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Openlane (NYSE:OPLN) EVP Charles Coleman Sells 38,769 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/openlane-nyseopln-evp-charles-coleman-sells-38769-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794499997.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Openlane (NYSE:OPLN) Director Sells $281,840.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/openlane-nyseopln-director-sells-281840-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794499996.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Raised Earnings Guidance Change OPENLANE (OPLN) Stock Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-opln/openlane/news/will-raised-earnings-guidance-change-openlane-opln-stock-nar","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482983.604,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"OPENLANE (NYSE: OPLN) marketplace president sells $2.84 million of stock after exercising options","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/openlane-nyse-opln-marketplace-president-sells-2-84-million-of-stock-after-exercising-options.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794276900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"OPENLANE (OPLN) Coul